00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
Boy Interrupted is a 2009 documentary film  on the life and death of Evan
Perry, who experienced bipolar depression from a young age.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
When  his parents, Dana and Hart Perry, consulted  psychiatrists about Evan's suicidal comments or other signs of depression, medical professionals did not
believe that he was mentally ill, and the footage was originally intended to show his symptoms and  help  access to the treatment he needed.

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
Evan was diagnosed with depression at age 5, and was
later diagnosed with bipolar depression.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
Despite the treatment and medication received, he
died by suicide in 2005 at age 15.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
Evan Perry had a family medical history involving serious mental illnesses.

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
The documentary  focuses on how his bipolar depression
affected him and those close to him.

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
About four years after Evan's death, the documentary was shown at the
Sundance Film Festival and released on television and DVD.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
